 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
   PITFALLS LOGGED DURING THIS ENGAGEMENT
 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

        * Single-instance target: a second launch forwards argv to the
          existing process and exits. An all-zero trace is then read as "the
          function never ran". Kill first, let the tracer own the spawn.
        * Byte-exact fingerprint compare: a "0x" prefix is a hard fail.
          Format errors masquerade as logic errors.
        * Never pipe evidence through `head` -- SIGPIPE can kill the sampled
          process mid-run and hand you a false negative.
        * A second, same-shaped pubkey constant exists in the plugin
          signature path (v0.28.1 VA 0x140BF8E25; 9/30 baseline VA 0x140B998DD).
           Same look, different job.
          Disambiguate by xref, not by shape.
        * Every address quoted in a report must trace back to evidence.
          Delete unverified ones; a plausible-but-wrong address is worse than
          no address at all.

