 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
   FIXING IT (vendor notes)
 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

        1. An equal-length-replaceable plaintext anchor is no anchor. Cover it
           with integrity (code-signing / cross-section hash), or ship it
           encrypted and unwrapped at runtime, or keep redundant copies and
           require they agree.
        2. Never anchor a grace deadline inside material the client can re-sign.
           Use an anti-rollback monotonic watermark that itself participates in
           the decision, or a server-signed timestamp.
        3. Reject future dates. |proof_date - now| beyond a threshold -> refuse.
        4. Untrusted / absent online recheck must downgrade, not fail-open.
        5. Device binding needs a key the client does not hold (HMAC/AEAD) or a
           hardware root of trust. FNV-1a of a registry GUID is a constant.
        6. Put every license.ini field under signature coverage, or delete it.
        7. Decouple policy from time: "lifetime updates" must not imply
           "expiry is not checked".

